menuconfig TFM_PARTITION_PROOF_OF_EXECUTION
    bool "Proof of Execution"
    depends on TFM_PARTITION_INITIAL_ATTESTATION
    default n

if TFM_PARTITION_PROOF_OF_EXECUTION

config POX_ALLOW_RUNTIME_KEY_OVERRIDE
    bool "Allow runtime override of the PoX signing key"
    default n
    help
      If enabled, compiles in pox_set_signing_key(), which lets a
      caller (e.g. a test partition) replace the hardcoded PoX
      signing key at runtime with a 32-byte ECDSA P-256 private
      scalar.

      Leave this disabled in production: the only signer should be
      the key hardcoded in pox_key.c.

config POX_ALLOW_PLACEHOLDER_KEY
    bool "Allow the placeholder PoX signing key (UNSAFE)"
    default n
    depends on TFM_BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG
    help
      The placeholder key shipped in pox_key.c is publicly known and
      must never be used in production. By default the build will fail
      with a hard error if the key has not been replaced.

      Enable this option ONLY for initial bring-up or CI builds where
      a real key is not yet available. It is intentionally restricted
      to debug builds (TFM_BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG) and cannot be set in
      release configurations.

      NEVER enable this on a production device.

endif
